Subject: [PATCH 56/56] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon: has_sparse, and the runs
 that earned it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 5 item 10 (sparse residency)
Why: patch 0022 set nvkmd_info::has_sparse false, and said why: NVK
 derives sparseBinding from cls_eng3d >= MAXWELL_B, GM20B's queried 3D
 class is exactly MAXWELL_B, and the feature would have been claimed on
 the strength of the chip while the layer had no way to unbind part of a
 reservation and leave the rest addressable. That was decision D12.
 .
 It was a statement about this driver, not about this hardware, and it
 has stopped being true. 0055 implements the two nvkmd operations that
 were missing; this is the line that turns them on.
 .
 It is one line and eight features. has_sparse gates sparseBinding,
 sparseResidencyBuffer, sparseResidencyImage2D and 3D, three
 multisample variants and sparseResidencyAliased
 (nvk_physical_device.c:395-402), and it makes NVK ask for a bind
 context — a third GPFIFO channel, where this driver was built around
 one. Both halves of that are why it is a commit of its own and why the
 evidence below is the whole Vulkan suite rather than the sparse test
 alone.
Evidence: RUN ON A CONSOLE 2026-08-24.
 .
 tests/t_vk_sparse.c, PASS 74/74 — D12's three questions asked through
 vkQueueBindSparse:
 .
   note MEASURED: the driver offers sparseBinding=true,
        sparseResidencyBuffer=true, sparseResidencyImage2D=true
   note MEASURED: the sparse block is 0x20000 bytes
   ok   MEASURED A: writing to an unbound sparse block did not lose the
        device
   ok   MEASURED B: the bound block holds what the GPU wrote (0 of 32768
        words wrong, first 0xc3c33c3c)
   note MEASURED C — D12 THROUGH VULKAN: after vkQueueBindSparse unbound
        the block, a write to it was swallowed. Sparse residency works
        through the whole stack, not only in horizon_gpu.
 .
 THE BIND CONTEXT DID NOT BREAK ANYTHING, which is the risk this flip
 actually carries. Every Vulkan test, same build, after the flip:
 t_vulkan 62/62, t_vk_transfer 203/203, t_vk_compute 37/37, t_vk_caps
 52/52, t_vk_image 72/72, t_vk_triangle 84/84, t_vk_depth 66/66,
 t_vk_texture 1685/1685, t_vk_format 282/282, t_vk_submits 287/287,
 t_vk_present_draw 183/183, t_vk_swapchain 143/143, t_vk_wsi_mt 71/71,
 t_vk_suboptimal 273/273, t_vk_immediate 442/442, t_vk_timestamp 60/60,
 t_vk_cache 43/43 cold and 45/45 warm. t_channel had already measured
 that 44 channels can be open at once, so the third one was affordable.
 .
 TWO OF THE EIGHT HAVE BEEN EXERCISED, and this does not pretend
 otherwise: sparseBinding and sparseResidencyBuffer, which are the two a
 buffer can reach. t_vk_caps asserts all eight are advertised, because
 one flag is what gates them and half appearing would mean something
 else had got in between — and its comment says which two the runs
 actually touched.
Upstream: no — it is a Horizon backend capability, measured on Horizon.

